{"title":"Angle Addition Formulas (Trigonometry)","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3b3cdf163a02f15e48258ceb43f00d1135892a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] real a,b,c; a=0.4924; b=0.5467; c=a+b; pair A,B,C,D,E,F; A=(0,0); D=(cos(c),sin(c)); B=(cos(a)*cos(b),0); C=(cos(a)*cos(b),sin(a)*cos(b)); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(A--C); E=foot(D,A,B); draw(D--E); F=foot(C,D,E); draw(C--F); draw(anglemark(B,A,C,4)); draw(anglemark(C,A,D,5.5)); label(&quot;$\\alpha$&quot;, A ,7*dir(a*30)); label(&quot;$\\beta$&quot;, A ,9*dir(b*45+ a*30)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,E); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,N); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,S); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,W); draw(rightanglemark(F,E,A,1)); draw(rightanglemark(C,F,D,1)); [/asy]\" width=\"225\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/278818c5d4550edbe1bacae656860522175d3119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC=\\alpha$\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/881cc2604a50550ba902492f44296bd6c55a860e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAD=\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd842e36ed64086a882c190267900ce65d1f7017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Sine_Angle_Addition\">Sine Angle Addition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Addition_Formulas_(Trigonometry)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Sine Angle Addition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6bb3a654ee1340140cffc62a08ef75f9ebe7422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=\\sin\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b6622cf836023236836db94a352340163dfac3b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=\\cos\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />. Furthermore, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b21a1ff4c3bee4552ca8d93eb14909e9e43df03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CDF=\\angle CAB=\\alpha$\" width=\"172\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/2/a52d666ab849f18ad901dfa35c2bbbf35a3a73cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE=BC=AC\\sin\\alpha=\\cos\\beta\\sin\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"279\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3eb4e7a973d91abe49db98c4d1e2803aa18d659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF=CD\\cos\\alpha=\\cos\\alpha\\sin\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"228\" height=\"16\" />. Thus, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/0/d70463ecfd76a2b3da8a481cd9ae7c93c0d8b2cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta)=DE=DF+FE=\\cos\\beta\\sin\\alpha+\\sin\\beta\\cos\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"444\" height=\"18\" />, giving<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93edc42b0c00d05642e7a04462d5951b6e9cd22d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta)=\\sin\\alpha\\cos\\beta+\\sin\\beta\\cos\\alpha.\\]\" width=\"288\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Cosine_Angle_Addition\">Cosine Angle Addition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Addition_Formulas_(Trigonometry)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Cosine Angle Addition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6bb3a654ee1340140cffc62a08ef75f9ebe7422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=\\sin\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/6/b6622cf836023236836db94a352340163dfac3b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=\\cos\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" />. Furthermore, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/2/5b21a1ff4c3bee4552ca8d93eb14909e9e43df03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CDF=\\angle CAB=\\alpha$\" width=\"172\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd78c889ce4bfb7d52e4c9ff3ba9dddf237d14dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC\\cos\\alpha=\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"227\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c8585d670abb404ebe24134c5c501c69bc158ce5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=CF=CD\\sin\\alpha=\\sin\\beta\\sin\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"276\" height=\"16\" />. Thus, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40ac8c3c2dbd94070ba135446556e10c90c8a93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta)=AE=AB-BE=\\cos\\beta\\cos\\alpha-\\sin\\beta\\sin\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"444\" height=\"20\" />, giving<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fb9fa74c8db644db0cfa6f909aba67bbb159998.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(\\alpha+\\beta)=\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta-\\sin\\beta\\sin\\alpha.\\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Tangent_Angle_Addition\">Tangent Angle Addition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Addition_Formulas_(Trigonometry)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Tangent Angle Addition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have already found <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> above; thus we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548b1d33b0f3080733c591c1f7cc7440fbba8627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\alpha+\\beta)=\\frac{\\sin\\alpha\\cos\\beta+\\sin\\beta\\cos\\alpha}{\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta-\\sin\\alpha\\sin\\beta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"292\" height=\"41\" />. Dividing numerator and denominator by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec6bda2854d2249817ae975acd8121289e130d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" />, we get<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/8/5c83dae35f8bcdfe414d572cdfc1186f9399d9bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan(\\alpha+\\beta)=\\frac{\\tan\\alpha+\\tan\\beta}{1-\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta}.\\]\" width=\"233\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Addition_Formulas_(Trigonometry)&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017172737\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 149/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 355/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6117/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.457      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.457      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13850:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017172737 and revision id 242206. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}